From 70a65c8911c2a6fb8c94b134e11e25ddfbfc20fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CC Stage2 <cc@iis.local>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 14:34:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] bid-radar-cron: zero-touch daily public-sector bid radar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pulls the CanadaBuys open-tender open-data CSV (free, no auth, no account),
filters to IT-relevant notices on title, de-dupes against a Netlify Blobs
index, and emails only genuinely new hits. Silence means nothing new.

Verified live: 887 notices scanned, 12 IT matches, 3.9s end to end.
Standing offers / supply arrangements (closing >365d out) are broken out
separately since those are continuous-qualification roster plays, not bids.

bids&tenders municipal portals are deliberately NOT scraped here: their
grids are client-rendered and every candidate RSS/JSON path 302s to an
error page. Those are covered by the scheduled browser sweep instead.

Uses `export const config = { schedule }` — never the legacy
`export default schedule(...)` wrapper that silently 502s in this project.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
